    "general_information": [
      {
        "type": "GeneralTitle",
        "content": "IMPORTANT MAJOR INFORMATION",
        "groupId": "83ba6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
        "position": 0,
        "area": "General"
      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralText",
        "content": "<p>The Russian Studies major allows students to learn the Russian language while studying economics, history, political science and other fields where Russian can be a plus.</p><p><br></p><p>Listed below are the lower division preparation courses for the major.</p><p><br></p><p>To be considered for this major, you must complete the following courses by the end of the spring before transfer:</p><ul><li>One year of college level Russian OR</li><li>At least one year of high school in which the primary language of instruction was Russian. </li></ul><p>Completion of two years of college level foreign language is <strong>STRONGLY RECOMMENDED</strong>. </p><p>A placement exam is required for all language majors regardless of credits earned in lower division language courses.</p><p>All courses must be taken for a letter grade.</p><p><br></p><p>For information regarding this major and UCLA's transfer selection process, visit <u style=\"color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\">https://slavic.ucla.edu</u> and <u style=\"color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\">https://admission.ucla.edu</u>.</p><p><br></p><p>PLEASE NOTE: the community college courses listed below have been approved to satisfy the preparation for this major at UCLA, but they may not be exact equivalents of the UCLA courses listed.</p>",
        "groupId": "85ba6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
        "position": 1,
        "area": "General"
      }
    ],
